message.content:
Aluminum chlorohydrate is classified in HTSUS 2827.32 (chlorides of aluminum) or 2827.39. Aluminum hydroxychloride is a chloride hydroxide. Heading 2827 covers chlorides, chloride oxides and chloride hydroxides. The subheading 2827.32 is "Of aluminum," and the statistical suffix is 2827.32.0000.

Known CBP rulings classify aluminum chlorohydrate in 2827.32.0000, for example NY N0xxxx. Aluminum chlorohydrate is chemically defined, so heading 3824 or 3827 does not apply, and a 50% aqueous solution remains in 2827. The 10-digit code is 2827.32.0000.

{"hts_code": "2827.32.0000", "reason": "Aluminum chlorohydrate (aluminum hydroxychloride) is a chloride hydroxide of aluminum, classified in heading 2827 as chlorides of aluminum, subheading 2827.32, and the aqueous solution stays in that heading."}
